version: "2.0"
name: gnomon-kernel-manifest
description: >-
  Mod manifests: loading and checking a mod manifest, its grants and grant lock,
  egress policy, layers, install snapshots, and the user MCP server manifest.
context:
  - >-
    Split out of packages/gnomon/.purpose (2026-10-27); path: values stay
    relative to packages/gnomon, the package root.
components:
  manifest-loader:
    description: >-
      Aegis final review: the grants lock is taken by linking a temp file
      holding pid:nonce (O_EXCL fallback where links are unsupported, L1); a
      deny over an install whose rows are written is refused (M3).
      TD-2026-10-20-514: prepareInstall (every check, rows BUILT with cardId,
      checked against the card's detail.rootRows) / commitInstall (token consumed,
      appendSignedGrantRows); buildGrantRow(s) and appendSignedGrantRows re-check
      every signed row under a cross-process lock file (grant-lock.ts: torn-tail
      repair, dir fsync, one in-flight root decision per home) and write once,
      grant.install last; the reader drops a cardId row whose batch anchor is
      missing (unanchored).
      S0b user-mcp.ts: userMcpServerNames(home, {repo?}) reads ONLY server NAMES
      (never commands, args or env) from ~/.claude.json (user scope mcpServers and
      local scope projects.<path>.mcpServers) and <repo>/.mcp.json (project scope,
      when a repo is given), fail-soft on a missing or unparseable file; fed to the
      install/decide/load COLLISION check so a mod's gm_<pub>_<name> server never
      collides with a server the user already has (Aegis S0b M1).
      #manifest-loader, the Desk (TD-2026-10-20-812). manifest.ts: provides.offers
      (offer-spec:v1 from gnomon-contracts, at most 6, unique kinds, needs a
      provides.mcp server since reach is mcp) and 'offers' in WIDENING_FIELDS (key
      kind@phase→handoffTool; a text-only change is no widening); a provides.mcp entry
      may declare a closed per-user override surface config{command?:true, args?:true,
      env?:[names]} (env names never PATH/HOME/NODE_OPTIONS/… nor LD_/DYLD_/ANTHROPIC_/
      CLAUDE_/GNOMON_/NPM_CONFIG_/GIT_; a config is part of the mcp widening key);
      validateMcpUserConfig + resolveMcpLaunch admit only what it declares, under
      COMMAND_UNSAFE (first-party servers launch as node <absolute path> from other
      repos; a user-set command is an absolute path, spawn with shell:false). Env
      names: MCP_ENV_DENY + MCP_ENV_DENY_PREFIXES (Aegis M1), and below first-party
      <NAME>_* or *_API_KEY / *_TOKEN only. Each offer contextIn source is its own
      widening key (kind:in:src). Not yet wired into a launch path. RESERVED_MOD_NAMES
      (kernel, gnomon, system, paradigm, claude, …; NAME at every tier), FIRST_PARTY_MOD_NAMES
      and FIRST_PARTY_NAME_PREFIXES (gnomon-, paradigm-, claude-, anthropic-) first-party only. install.ts surfaceOf: one 'offer:' card line per offer and a
      'user may set:' suffix on an mcp line; both absent when undeclared, so pre-812
      card detail hashes are unchanged.
      #manifest-loader + policy (spec §3.6, §4.3, §12.5, §15.4, §15.5, §15.7,
      §16; §19.1 M1.5). src/kernel/manifest/. manifest.ts — manifest:v1
      validation, producer-strict and fail-closed (wire form: the JSON subset
      of the §4.3 YAML in gnomon-manifest.json, zero deps): unknown keys and
      trust:/source:/postinstall refused; kind: mod needs abi mod-abi:v1, an
      unknown abi refused; a name equal to a kernel namespace token refused;
      kind adapter/provider first-party only, a provider ships only
      provides.knowledge; tool effects ⊆ read|write|network|spend; card.* and
      status.mod slots append-only; events under modns.<name>.*; keybindings
      bind declared commands, never the reserved decision keys; capabilities
      are §15.4 forms (approve/band:write never; voice.approve:<class> never
      from a manifest; knowledge:federate/link:send first-party only;
      log.append only on its own modns); provides.knowledge needs
      knowledge:provide and never egress. manifestHash = sha256(canonical
      JSON); detectWidening = additions by field (effects, egress,
      capabilities, events, tools, views, commands, keybindings, knowledge).
      egress.ts — Anthropic hosts (anthropic.com, claude.ai, claude.com and
      subdomains, and any wildcard covering them) refused in manifests and
      grant rows (G-MAN-01). snapshot.ts — the snapshot copier: copies a
      package or linked folder to <home>/mods/<name>/pinned/<hex>/ (owner-only,
      read-only), packageHash over the sorted tree of the COPY (exact bytes,
      .git skipped unread), refusing symlink/junction, hardlink (nlink > 1),
      .node addon, a path escaping the folder, special files, case-colliding
      paths and a swap between walk and read (fstat dev/ino), emitting
      mod.snapshot.refused + manifest.refuse{SNAPSHOT}; lockfile rule
      (node_modules needs an npm lockfile, the card lists every
      package@version; other formats refused, LOCKFILE); lifecycle install
      scripts refused (POSTINSTALL); diffTrees for the re-approve card.
      grants.ts — <home>/grants.jsonl, root-signed rows through the
      RootAuthority seam (production refuses until M1.3), fail-closed reader
      (unsigned, untrusted signer, bad signature, unknown kind, malformed,
      Anthropic egress, egress beside knowledge:provide → rejected[]);
      grant.install carries `name` beside the §15.4 fields; the effective pin
      is the last grant.install row. install.ts — stageInstall (package or
      linked) raises a PENDING card:v1 kind install with its detail (name,
      source, tier, effects, egress, capabilities, events, tools, views, read
      paths, package@version list, widening, file diff, stagedBy) and signs
      nothing (manifest.staged). The kernel-composed line `runs commands: N
      mcp server(s), M hook(s)` follows the packageHash line, before any
      manifest-controlled line (Aegis round 2 C2); mcp.command, mcp.args,
      hooks.command and hooks.event refuse SCHEMA on C0/C1, Zl, Zp and Cf
      (U+2028/U+2029 would otherwise draw a fake card line, C1); a linked
      source whose realpath has such a character is refused SCHEMA at stage
      and INTEGRITY at re-derivation, and the header is one display line
      (version and source middle-truncated for display; contentHash keeps
      the full detail), so the count line is always index 2 (Aegis round 3). The card's lines put every mcp server and
      every hook on its OWN line and are sanitized and WRAPPED by code points
      under the broker's MAX_LINE (continuations `  ↳ `), never cut, so a long
      mcp argument list cannot push a hook out of sight; the sanitizer flags
      travel with the lines (blockFor → rederiveInstallDetail → the broker),
      and contentHash still covers the full detail (T-2026-10-18-015 item 2);
      loadMod loads only from a pinned snapshot
      under a root-signed grant.install, re-hashes it (INTEGRITY), checks
      grants, and for a linked folder re-hashes the source: a change pauses
      the mod (mod.paused) and stages one re-approve card (manifest.widened
      when widened). The card DECISION and the human rollback (re-pin a
      previously approved snapshot, mod.rolled-back) are module-private and
      registered only on the internal seam channel (slot `manifest`), reached
      only through src/kernel/testing.ts (decideInstallCard,
      rollbackModSnapshot) until the M1.6 approval broker owns cards; both
      need a PresenceToken (mod.install / mod.rollback) and a signing root.
      layers.ts — layersHash (managed, user settings*.json + CLAUDE.md +
      skills/plugins/agents/commands listings, project and worktree .claude/**
      + CLAUDE.md + CLAUDE.local.md) and gitHash (.git/config, hooks/**,
      info/** in the common dir, a worktree's .git file followed,
      .gitattributes), CRLF→LF and case-folded NFC path keys on every platform
      (G-WIN-04). policy.ts — the per-session policy DATA for the `session`
      profile (keys/Warpline-token/browser read denies, ~/.gnomon + settings
      layers + linked folders write denies, endpoint-port loopback deny,
      process-info deny-others, launchers deny; realpath'd; policyHash) and the
      matching policy.json permissions block — the platform profile is
      generated by M1.7. generate.ts — plugin.json, .mcp.json, hooks.json and
      .gnomon/.gitignore from a kind: distro manifest into the repo's
      .gnomon/, each with a marker and a ledger; a fixed point; never
      overwrites a file that is not ours; uninstallRepo removes exactly the
      ledger's unedited files and the dirs it created (project.yaml stays);
      uninstallHome removes ~/.gnomon or returns it as the export path.
      ROUND 2 (review + Aegis F1–F11): generate.ts confines every path to the
      fixed generated set under <repo>/.gnomon (lstat each component, refuse
      links/junctions, realpath inside .gnomon, temp file O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW +
      rename) and keys ownership on the manifestHash marker plus the
      kernel-held record <home>/generated/<sha256(realpath repo)>.json (the
      repo holds no ledger); the session policy write-denies the whole
      ~/.claude/** and ~/.claude.json (both also hashed into layersHash — a
      gap in spec §3.3/§15.5 to amend) and .git/hooks|config|info (gitHash
      inputs; §15.5 amendment), and carries the platform-neutral deny classes
      (tmux/screen sockets, helper IPC, sysmond, AppleEvents, service
      manager, mic/camera, launchers) mapped per platform in
      src/platform/session-denies.ts; widening covers mcp and hooks and the
      card lists commands, keybindings, knowledge, mcp, hooks and opaque
      array counts; the lockfile rule is case-folded, applies at any depth
      and cross-checks shipped package.json versions; the tier is derived
      (linked ⇒ local, first-party only from a bundled packageHash allowlist,
      empty for now; a signed claim is refused until trusted keys exist);
      decideInstall validates the cardId, recomputes contentHash, re-derives
      the detail from the pinned snapshot, appends grant.install LAST and is
      idempotent; egress refuses ports, numeric hosts, single labels and
      local/private names; symlinked layers hash the target bytes and
      .claude/worktrees/ is excluded. The case-collision oracle is
      exercised on Linux CI (a case-insensitive FS cannot hold the pair).
      Events: §9.1 kinds only (manifest.*, mod.*); the spec declares no
      signals. Refusals are refusal:v1 with data.manifestCode (not
      data.reason, which would move clientApiId).
    path: src/kernel/manifest/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, manifest, policy, paradigm-8, m1.5]
    tests:
      - test/manifest-offers.test.ts
      - test/manifest-loader.test.ts
      - test/seams-fence.test.ts
    oracles: [G-MAN-01, G-MAN-02, G-MAN-03, G-HON-04, G-LAW-04, G-WIN-04]
